  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Study visit on child care rehabilitation centers from Ukraine to the Netherlands (Part I)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project supports the logistics to implement a seven-days study visit on child care for ten representatives of Ukrainian organisations to the Netherlands. In doing so, it enables that the delegation gets practical understanding of the Dutch requirements for the gradation of different types of rehabilitation facilities; and the rehabilitation methods concerning the mental and physical rehabilitation of children and addressing oncology care.  The study visit is being organised by the Task Force Health Care as part of the prioritised activities of the Dutch Public-Private Platform on Life Science and Health of the Netherlands for Ukraine. Aim of this visit is to support the public and private (healthcare) sector in Ukraine through showcasing Dutch best practices, exchanging knowledge, inspiring delegates and networking with focus on childcare rehabilitation.</narrative>
  </description>
